00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:54,440
 I'll just, I'll finish kind of explaining how I read

365
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,440
 how it defines control more generally.

366
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,600
 So the other thing it says is,

367
00:15:57,600 --> 00:16:01,840
 if you can do something like pause or restart trading,

368
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,240
 if you have discretion to do that,

369
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:06,400
 that could potentially fall under the standard of control.

370
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:10,680
 And then the third category is about user interfaces

371
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:13,360
 or front-ends, right? So like websites or apps

372
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,880
 that allow you to access the DeFi protocol.

373
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:19,200
 And the question there is, can you restrict who can trade?

374
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:22,320
 Do you exercise discretion over which assets

375
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:26,020
 or pools or strategies that users can have access to?

376
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:30,160
 Can you intervene in execution and do you route orders

377
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:33,600
 or somehow like materially modify the outcome, right?

378
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,240
 So I have a few thoughts on this.

379
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,800
 First is a substantive one,

